    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx);
}
```
Reason:
The code incorrectly assumes that the `ctx` field is always present in the `ssh_cipher_struct`, which is only true when `HAVE_LIBCRYPTO` is defined. If this macro is not defined, `cipher->ctx` may not exist, leading to a potential dereference of a NULL pointer when calling `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef HAVE_LIBCRYPTO
if (cipher->ctx != NULL) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx);
}
#endif
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the call to `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free` is only made when `HAVE_LIBCRYPTO` is defined and `cipher->ctx` is non-NULL, thus preventing any dereference of a NULL pointer and maintaining the integrity of the code across different build configurations.

